# Lines no test on this machine can reach, one per line: "<path> -- <why>".
#
# A path with no reason fails `make lint`, and the whole list is capped at 3% of statements by
# `make cover`. "Unreachable by design" is not a reason: a line no test can reach is either dead
# code, which is deleted, or a missing test, which is written.
#
# A platform file is not compiled on this host, so it has no statements in the profile at all:
# it is outside the denominator and outside the 3%. The cap is for code that is compiled and
# reachable, which is exactly the code that must not be excluded.

internal/sandbox/nested_darwin.go -- platform: only compiled on darwin, cannot run on the CI host
internal/sandbox/nested_other.go -- platform: only compiled off darwin
internal/sandbox/kvm_other.go -- platform: only compiled off linux
internal/sandbox/lock_other.go -- platform: only compiled off unix
internal/sandbox/runtime_other.go -- platform: only compiled off unix
internal/netns/netns_other.go -- platform: only compiled off linux
cmd/acornd/setupcred_other.go -- platform: credentials come from the OS keyring, linux only
cmd/acornd/tty_other.go -- platform: terminal handling is a unix syscall, windows only
